          "In addressing the operational nuances of Part 1, In modern enterprise supply chains, AI-driven demand forecasting represents the catalyst for operational synchronization. Traditional moving averages and univariate spreadsheet models operate with blinders, unable to capture multi-scale seasonality, promotional cross-elasticity, or macroeconomic indicators. When consumer demand fluctuates unpredictably, rigid replenishment models trigger severe stockouts on fast-moving SKUs while accumulating millions of dollars in dead inventory across slow-moving lines.",
