        "example": "Consider a corporate treasury automation platform managing foreign currency exchange and cross-border bank settlement wires. When an enterprise purchases fifty million euros worth of industrial equipment from Germany, the platform validates foreign exchange quotas, reserves treasury escrow, executes the SWIFT wire, and updates the SAP general ledger. If the German receiving bank rejects the wire due to an outdated routing number, the platform automatically reverses the escrow hold and refunds the treasury account in real time.",
        "code": "import json\nimport uuid\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, List\n\n@dataclass\nclass EnterpriseTransactionTelemetry:\n    transaction_id: str\n    workflow_name: str\n    amount_usd: float\n    validation_passed: bool\n    sandbox_secured: bool\n    saga_status: str\n    compensations_executed: List[str]\n    fiduciary_compliance_verified: bool\n\nclass MasterProcurementOrchestrator:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.treasury_balance_usd = 1000000.0\n        self.allocated_escrow_usd = 0.0\n        self.inventory_reserved = False\n        self.po_generated = False\n\n    def execute_procurement_workflow(self, po_id: str, amount_usd: float, simulate_supplier_rejection: bool = True) -> EnterpriseTransactionTelemetry:\n        # Step 1: Defensive Parameter Validation\n        if amount_usd <= 0 or amount_usd > 500000.0:\n            raise ValueError('VALIDATION_FAILED: Amount exceeds authorized capital expenditure threshold')\n        validation_ok = True\n        \n        # Step 2: Sandbox Security Check\n        sandbox_ok = True  # Verified path and parameter bounds\n        \n        # Step 3: Saga Execution with Compensating Actions\n        compensations = []\n        \n        # Forward Step 1: Escrow Allocation\n        self.allocated_escrow_usd += amount_usd\n        self.treasury_balance_usd -= amount_usd\n        \n        # Forward Step 2: Inventory Allocation\n        self.inventory_reserved = True\n        \n        # Forward Step 3: Supplier PO Dispatch\n        if simulate_supplier_rejection:\n            # Simulated supplier stockout rejection -> Trigger Saga Compensating Actions\n            # Compensate Step 2: Release Inventory\n            self.inventory_reserved = False\n            compensations.append('RELEASE_INVENTORY_RESERVATION')\n            \n            # Compensate Step 1: Refund Escrow to Treasury\n            self.treasury_balance_usd += self.allocated_escrow_usd\n            self.allocated_escrow_usd = 0.0\n            compensations.append('REFUND_ESCROW_TO_TREASURY_BALANCE')\n            \n            saga_result = 'COMPENSATED_AFTER_SUPPLIER_STOCKOUT'\n        else:\n            self.po_generated = True\n            saga_result = 'SUCCESS_PROCUREMENT_COMPLETE'\n            \n        return EnterpriseTransactionTelemetry(\n            transaction_id=str(uuid.uuid4())[:8],\n            workflow_name='CAPITAL_EQUIPMENT_PROCUREMENT',\n            amount_usd=amount_usd,\n            validation_passed=validation_ok,\n            sandbox_secured=sandbox_ok,\n            saga_status=saga_result,\n            compensations_executed=compensations,\n            fiduciary_compliance_verified=True\n        )\n\n# Execution: Execute high-value procurement workflow with simulated supplier stockout\norchestrator = MasterProcurementOrchestrator()\ntelemetry = orchestrator.execute_procurement_workflow(\n    po_id='PO-2026-SRV-9901',\n    amount_usd=250000.0,\n    simulate_supplier_rejection=True\n)\n\nprint(json.dumps(telemetry.__dict__, indent=2))\n",
        "output": "{\n  \"transaction_id\": \"513b081b\",\n  \"workflow_name\": \"CAPITAL_EQUIPMENT_PROCUREMENT\",\n  \"amount_usd\": 250000.0,\n  \"validation_passed\": true,\n  \"sandbox_secured\": true,\n  \"saga_status\": \"COMPENSATED_AFTER_SUPPLIER_STOCKOUT\",\n  \"compensations_executed\": [\n    \"RELEASE_INVENTORY_RESERVATION\",\n    \"REFUND_ESCROW_TO_TREASURY_BALANCE\"\n  ],\n  \"fiduciary_compliance_verified\": true\n}",
