        "example": "Consider an international consortium of central banks verifying the physical gold reserves stored in an underground vault. Five independent auditing firms inspect the vault simultaneously. If up to one of the auditing firms is bribed or compromised by an adversary and submits a falsified report claiming the vault is empty, the four honest firms reach unanimous 4-out-of-5 consensus, mathematically isolating the rogue auditor and certifying true reserve holdings.",
        "code": "import json\nimport math\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Tuple\n\n@dataclass\nclass AgentVoteReport:\n    agent_id: str\n    risk_score_estimate: float  # Scale 0.0 (Safe) to 100.0 (Extreme Risk)\n    reputation_score: float     # 0.0 to 1.0\n    digital_signature_valid: bool\n\nclass EnterprisePBFTConsensusEngine:\n    def __init__(self, max_tolerated_byzantine_faults: int = 2):\n        self.f = max_tolerated_byzantine_faults\n        self.min_required_nodes = 3 * self.f + 1\n\n    def evaluate_byzantine_consensus(self, reports: List[AgentVoteReport]) -> Dict:\n        total_nodes = len(reports)\n        if total_nodes < self.min_required_nodes:\n            return {\n                'status': 'INSUFFICIENT_NODES_FOR_BFT',\n                'required_nodes': self.min_required_nodes,\n                'actual_nodes': total_nodes\n            }\n            \n        # Step 1: Filter invalid cryptographic signatures (Sybil defense)\n        authenticated_reports = [r for r in reports if r.digital_signature_valid]\n        if len(authenticated_reports) < (2 * self.f + 1):\n            return {'status': 'FAILED_AUTHENTICATION_THRESHOLD'}\n            \n        # Step 2: Statistical Outlier Isolation (Median Absolute Deviation)\n        scores = [r.risk_score_estimate for r in authenticated_reports]\n        scores_sorted = sorted(scores)\n        median = scores_sorted[len(scores_sorted) // 2]\n        \n        # Outlier threshold: absolute deviation > 25.0 points from median\n        honest_nodes = []\n        byzantine_nodes = []\n        \n        for r in authenticated_reports:\n            deviation = abs(r.risk_score_estimate - median)\n            if deviation > 25.0:\n                byzantine_nodes.append({'agent_id': r.agent_id, 'outlier_score': r.risk_score_estimate, 'deviation': deviation})\n            else:\n                honest_nodes.append(r)\n                \n        # Step 3: Reputation-Weighted Consensus across Honest Nodes\n        total_weight = sum(r.reputation_score for r in honest_nodes)\n        weighted_consensus_score = sum(r.risk_score_estimate * r.reputation_score for r in honest_nodes) / total_weight\n        \n        return {\n            'bft_status': 'BYZANTINE_CONSENSUS_CERTIFIED',\n            'total_nodes_participating': total_nodes,\n            'max_tolerable_faults': self.f,\n            'isolated_byzantine_count': len(byzantine_nodes),\n            'isolated_byzantine_nodes': byzantine_nodes,\n            'honest_nodes_count': len(honest_nodes),\n            'median_score': median,\n            'reputation_weighted_consensus': round(weighted_consensus_score, 2),\n            'consensus_adjudication': 'APPROVED_LOW_RISK' if weighted_consensus_score < 30.0 else 'REJECTED_HIGH_RISK'\n        }\n\n# Execution: 7 nodes (N=7 >= 3*2 + 1 = 7). 2 Byzantine nodes injecting extreme falsified risk scores.\nreports = [\n    AgentVoteReport('HONEST_NODE_1', 18.5, 0.95, True),\n    AgentVoteReport('HONEST_NODE_2', 20.0, 0.90, True),\n    AgentVoteReport('HONEST_NODE_3', 19.2, 0.98, True),\n    AgentVoteReport('HONEST_NODE_4', 21.5, 0.88, True),\n    AgentVoteReport('HONEST_NODE_5', 18.0, 0.92, True),\n    # Byzantine Nodes attempting to sabotage loan approval\n    AgentVoteReport('BYZANTINE_NODE_6', 95.0, 0.60, True),  # Malicious outlier high\n    AgentVoteReport('BYZANTINE_NODE_7', 98.0, 0.55, True)   # Malicious outlier high\n]\n\nengine = EnterprisePBFTConsensusEngine(max_tolerated_byzantine_faults=2)\nconsensus_result = engine.evaluate_byzantine_consensus(reports)\nprint(json.dumps(consensus_result, indent=2))\n",
        "output": "{\n  \"bft_status\": \"BYZANTINE_CONSENSUS_CERTIFIED\",\n  \"total_nodes_participating\": 7,\n  \"max_tolerable_faults\": 2,\n  \"isolated_byzantine_count\": 2,\n  \"isolated_byzantine_nodes\": [\n    {\n      \"agent_id\": \"BYZANTINE_NODE_6\",\n      \"outlier_score\": 95.0,\n      \"deviation\": 75.0\n    },\n    {\n      \"agent_id\": \"BYZANTINE_NODE_7\",\n      \"outlier_score\": 98.0,\n      \"deviation\": 78.0\n    }\n  ],\n  \"honest_nodes_count\": 5,\n  \"median_score\": 20.0,\n  \"reputation_weighted_consensus\": 19.41,\n  \"consensus_adjudication\": \"APPROVED_LOW_RISK\"\n}",
