        "example": "Consider the Chief Audit Executive of a global financial institution preparing for an annual regulatory examination by the Federal Reserve. The executive queries the internal AI system for 'Mandatory escalation procedures when a liquidity ratio falls below minimum regulatory capital thresholds'. The hierarchical RAG pipeline retrieves a 40-word child chunk, expands it into the 2,000-word parent chapter on Liquidity Risk Governance, compresses out unrelated collateral margin rules, and formats a pristine 200-word golden prompt containing the exact statutory notification deadlines and board escalation steps.",
        "code": "import json\nimport math\nimport re\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, asdict\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Tuple\n\n@dataclass\nclass ParentDocumentRecord:\n    parent_id: str\n    title: str\n    full_content: str\n    category: str\n\n@dataclass\nclass ChildChunkRecord:\n    child_id: str\n    parent_id: str\n    snippet: str\n    embedding: List[float]\n\nclass MasterHierarchicalRAGPipeline:\n    def __init__(self, compression_threshold: float = 0.45):\n        self.compression_threshold = compression_threshold\n        self.parent_store = {} # parent_id -> ParentDocumentRecord\n        self.child_index = []  # List[ChildChunkRecord]\n\n    def ingest_document(self, parent: ParentDocumentRecord, child_snippets: List[Tuple[str, List[float]]]):\n        self.parent_store[parent.parent_id] = parent\n        for idx, (snippet, emb) in enumerate(child_snippets, start=1):\n            child_rec = ChildChunkRecord(\n                child_id=f'{parent.parent_id}-C{idx:02d}',\n                parent_id=parent.parent_id,\n                snippet=snippet,\n                embedding=self._normalize(emb)\n            )\n            self.child_index.append(child_rec)\n\n    def execute_hierarchical_retrieval(self, query: str, query_emb: List[float], top_children: int = 2) -> Dict:\n        norm_q = self._normalize(query_emb)\n        scored_children = []\n        \n        # Phase 1: Surgical child chunk vector search\n        for child in self.child_index:\n            cosine = sum(q * c for q, c in zip(norm_q, child.embedding))\n            scored_children.append((child, cosine))\n            \n        scored_children.sort(key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)\n        top_matches = scored_children[:top_children]\n        \n        # Phase 2: Small-to-Big Parent Expansion & Deduplication\n        resolved_parents = {}\n        for child, score in top_matches:\n            p_id = child.parent_id\n            if p_id not in resolved_parents:\n                resolved_parents[p_id] = self.parent_store[p_id]\n                \n        # Phase 3: Contextual Compression of Parent Documents\n        compressed_payloads = []\n        total_raw_words = 0\n        total_compressed_words = 0\n        \n        for parent in resolved_parents.values():\n            raw_words = len(parent.full_content.split())\n            total_raw_words += raw_words\n            \n            sentences = [s.strip() for s in re.split(r'(?<=[.!?])\\s+', parent.full_content) if s.strip()]\n            retained = []\n            for s in sentences:\n                # Check semantic alignment and keyword presence\n                s_lower = s.lower()\n                is_relevant = any(w in s_lower for w in ['escalation', 'liquidity', 'capital', 'threshold', 'hours', 'board', 'regulator'])\n                if is_relevant:\n                    retained.append(s)\n                    \n            compressed_text = ' '.join(retained)\n            comp_words = len(compressed_text.split())\n            total_compressed_words += comp_words\n            \n            compressed_payloads.append({\n                'parent_id': parent.parent_id,\n                'title': parent.title,\n                'category': parent.category,\n                'original_words': raw_words,\n                'compressed_words': comp_words,\n                'extracted_context': compressed_text\n            })\n            \n        token_savings = round((1.0 - (total_compressed_words / total_raw_words)) * 100.0, 2) if total_raw_words > 0 else 0.0\n        \n        return {\n            'query': query,\n            'top_child_match_id': top_matches[0][0].child_id,\n            'child_cosine_similarity': round(top_matches[0][1], 4),\n            'resolved_parent_count': len(resolved_parents),\n            'total_raw_words': total_raw_words,\n            'total_compressed_words': total_compressed_words,\n            'overall_token_savings_pct': token_savings,\n            'compressed_golden_context': compressed_payloads\n        }\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _normalize(v: List[float]) -> List[float]:\n        norm = math.sqrt(sum(x * x for x in v))\n        return [x / norm for x in v] if norm > 0 else v\n\n# Execution: Processing Enterprise Statutory Banking Liquidity Standards\npipeline = MasterHierarchicalRAGPipeline()\n\nparent_doc = ParentDocumentRecord(\n    parent_id='DOC-BANK-LIQ-901',\n    title='Enterprise Capital & Liquidity Ratio Escalation Mandate',\n    full_content=(\n        \"The bank operates primary and secondary data centers with triple-redundant fiber optic connections to ensure trading uptime. \"\n        \"In accordance with Basel III frameworks, the institution must maintain a Liquidity Coverage Ratio (LCR) exceeding 100 percent. \"\n        \"If the projected liquidity ratio falls below the 105 percent internal buffer threshold, the Chief Risk Officer must be alerted immediately. \"\n        \"Facility maintenance managers must test diesel backup electrical generators on the first Sunday of every calendar month. \"\n        \"Formal written escalation to the Board of Directors and the Federal Reserve must occur within twenty-four hours of an official breach. \"\n        \"Cafeteria vendor catering invoices are settled on net-30 terms through the accounts payable automated workflow engine.\"\n    ),\n    category='REGULATORY_PRUDENTIAL_STANDARDS'\n)\n\n# Granular child chunks for vector indexing\nchild_snippets = [\n    (\"Liquidity Coverage Ratio (LCR) must exceed 100 percent under Basel III frameworks.\", [0.82, 0.20, 0.45, 0.15]),\n    (\"Liquidity breach escalation to Board and Federal Reserve required within 24 hours.\", [0.90, 0.15, 0.55, 0.20])\n]\npipeline.ingest_document(parent_doc, child_snippets)\n\nquery = 'regulatory escalation timeline when bank liquidity ratio falls below threshold'\nq_vec = [0.88, 0.18, 0.52, 0.18]\n\nretrieval_report = pipeline.execute_hierarchical_retrieval(query, q_vec, top_children=1)\nprint(json.dumps(retrieval_report, indent=2))\n",
        "output": "{\n  \"query\": \"regulatory escalation timeline when bank liquidity ratio falls below threshold\",\n  \"top_child_match_id\": \"DOC-BANK-LIQ-901-C02\",\n  \"child_cosine_similarity\": 0.9993,\n  \"resolved_parent_count\": 1,\n  \"total_raw_words\": 110,\n  \"total_compressed_words\": 60,\n  \"overall_token_savings_pct\": 45.45,\n  \"compressed_golden_context\": [\n    {\n      \"parent_id\": \"DOC-BANK-LIQ-901\",\n      \"title\": \"Enterprise Capital & Liquidity Ratio Escalation Mandate\",\n      \"category\": \"REGULATORY_PRUDENTIAL_STANDARDS\",\n      \"original_words\": 110,\n      \"compressed_words\": 60,\n      \"extracted_context\": \"In accordance with Basel III frameworks, the institution must maintain a Liquidity Coverage Ratio (LCR) exceeding 100 percent. If the projected liquidity ratio falls below the 105 percent internal buffer threshold, the Chief Risk Officer must be alerted immediately. Formal written escalation to the Board of Directors and the Federal Reserve must occur within twenty-four hours of an official breach.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
