          "why": "Unfused kernels incur high launch overhead and constantly flush intermediate activation tensors to external DRAM. Kernel fusion keeps data in on-chip SRAM, drastically lowering memory bandwidth demand.",
          "explanation": "Unfused kernels incur high launch overhead and constantly flush intermediate activation tensors to external DRAM. Kernel fusion keeps data in on-chip SRAM, drastically lowering memory bandwidth demand."
